window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Award-Winning Kindle Vella Fall Madness 2023</b></p> <p><b>Top Faved in SciFi-Fantasy-Romance</b></p> <p><b>Mature Audiences:</b></p> <p><b>DARIUS:</b></p> <p>There she lay in all her glory...it was her: Dalia from the Wild.</p> <p>As she lay upon the manicured turf eating a fresh peach under a heavy tree, my mouth salivated as she sexily consumed her delicacy.</p> <p>She was unaware I stood there as I cocked my head to admire that lovely unspoiled girl.</p> <p>Her long golden locks spiraled all around her while her wet lips suctioned on that tempting fruit.</p> <p>Her eyelashes to her pink freckled cheeks...she was like sunshine in the shadows, as if in a forbidden garden.</p> <p><b>I, as sweet as Lucifer, would snake my way into her thoughts with mere words. Words of truths she had yet to know.</b></p> <p>Was this truly the Wild Cherry the Workfolk Guardians had fought that night to check her virtue?</p> <p>Was this Dalia the one who had escaped the Workfolk trade, still untouched?</p> <p><b>I grinned devilishly at the hen that would lay the golden eggs that could heal our land and cure my father.</b></p> <p>Her tart and seductive responses were fresh and challenging.</p> <p>But how?</p> <p>How would I steal her from Dr. Lord Kaine Remmington's fortified residence?</p> <p>I would find a way. Truly it was Dalia's blood that ruled, for he who had her had immense power over all of Hearth.</p> <p><b>Dalia's blood reigned...She would be mine.</b></p> <p><b>KAINE:</b></p> <p>Desperate, I traveled from Eden, the highest kingdom on Hearth, searching for Sabrina's offspring who could carry a DNA link and cure.</p> <p>I was venturing into the Wild, far from our cities to the slum boroughs.</p> <p>Would Sabrina and her sister, Delila, have given up life in Eden to live in squalor &amp; birth a royal baby in utter poverty? Those in the Wild lived like the mythical Vikings without any crude weaponry. Their struggle to survive was real.</p> <p><b>I would send the Workfolk Guardians...</b></p> <p><b><i>Not...a...dull...moment</i></b>!</p> <p><b>Triggers</b></p>"; 
